                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make like a devil; to invest with the character of a devil."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "289e12f3-4b4a-34c5-a37d-bcc08fed8fe8",
                                        "entry_id": "95273d59-a143-37b4-acf9-31d29563a06f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To annoy or bother."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d133a1b0-480a-3e06-ac15-79125adf6c89",
                                        "entry_id": "95273d59-a143-37b4-acf9-31d29563a06f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To work as a ‘devil’; to work for a lawyer or writer without fee or recognition."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f21317ed-c571-4cf1-8e6f-d6a87411c9d0",
                                                "sense_id": "d133a1b0-480a-3e06-ac15-79125adf6c89",
                                                "text": "He did not repeat the scathing estimate of her character by Quatrefages, who at that time spent one afternoon a week devilling at the Consulate, keeping the petty-cash box in order."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0a8f7b33-07ad-3094-889a-acfb0f3d493c",
                                        "entry_id": "95273d59-a143-37b4-acf9-31d29563a06f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To ghostwrite; to author while working as a ‘devil’."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d08a8ac-c708-4ddd-a6a2-d34bf44ba7cb",
                                                "sense_id": "0a8f7b33-07ad-3094-889a-acfb0f3d493c",
                                                "text": "Didn't secretaries write the speeches of Parliamentary \"big-bugs\"? Weren't the opinions of eminent lawyers often written by their juniors, read over and signed? Weren't briefs and pleadings devilled?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a6c704bf-42f4-3822-adfe-7897d0e18c4f",
                                        "entry_id": "95273d59-a143-37b4-acf9-31d29563a06f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To prepare (food) with spices, making it spicy:",
                                            "To grill with cayenne pepper; to season highly in cooking, as with pepper."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e34834e2-8240-45c9-b9f0-57e5b0dac3db",
                                                "sense_id": "a6c704bf-42f4-3822-adfe-7897d0e18c4f",
                                                "text": "[…]; you could watch a buckwheat pancake whirled into existence under your eyes and see fowls' legs devilled, peppered, grilled, and tormented till they lost all semblance of the original Mariposa chicken."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7782430d-f02a-3441-ba9c-16b41f079ad4",
                                        "entry_id": "95273d59-a143-37b4-acf9-31d29563a06f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To prepare (food) with spices, making it spicy:",
                                            "To finely grind cooked ham or other meat with spices and condiments."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
